+# Flags Fallback
+
+## Purpose
+
+Defines what a server SDK does when a local evaluation cannot produce a conclusive result.
+
+## Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Inconclusive local results fall back to the remote endpoint
+
+When a local evaluation is inconclusive for any cause, the SDK MUST request that flag from the `/flags` endpoint and return the remote result, unless the caller enabled local-only mode. In local-only mode the SDK MUST return the flag as unresolved.
+
+#### Scenario: Fallback after an inconclusive local result
+
+- **WHEN** local evaluation of flag `beta` is inconclusive and local-only mode is off
+- **THEN** the SDK requests `beta` from `/flags` and returns the remote value
+
+#### Scenario: Local-only mode
+
+- **WHEN** local evaluation of flag `beta` is inconclusive and local-only mode is on
+- **THEN** the SDK returns `beta` as unresolved and sends no request to `/flags`
+
+### Requirement: One remote request per evaluation call
+
+When several flags in one evaluation call fall back, the SDK MUST request them together in a single `/flags` request.
+
+#### Scenario: Two flags fall back together
+
+- **WHEN** flags `beta` and `gamma` are both inconclusive in one call to evaluate all flags
+- **THEN** the SDK sends one `/flags` request that covers both flags
